WEBVTT

00:00.220 --> 00:05.440
<b>Fall!</b>

00:00.530 --> 00:01.890
Fall!

00:01.560 --> 00:05.440
<b>Fall!</b>

00:02.220 --> 00:03.720
Fall!

00:03.850 --> 00:05.440
<b>Fall!</b>

00:03.990 --> 00:05.430
Fall!

00:05.710 --> 00:10.680
Fall!

00:27.360 --> 00:28.170
You're joking...

00:29.980 --> 00:31.120
No...

00:32.350 --> 00:33.580
It won't come out.

00:34.350 --> 00:36.100
Do not blame yourself.

00:36.380 --> 00:38.570
This is but our fate.

00:38.850 --> 00:42.600
<b>Bungo Stray Dogs</b>

00:39.940 --> 00:42.600
Final trajectory confirmation complete.

00:42.850 --> 00:44.940
Impact in T-30 seconds.

00:45.360 --> 00:48.890
Targeting 30 million cities. No amendments.

00:50.260 --> 00:52.390
The world's ending.

00:53.660 --> 00:55.070
Oh, God...

01:03.790 --> 01:04.940
Why...

01:05.630 --> 01:09.000
It was for neither a lack of 
courage nor a lack of ability.

01:11.080 --> 01:13.330
You did nothing wrong.

01:13.950 --> 01:15.870
Just a lack of weight.

01:16.650 --> 01:18.420
Nothing more.

01:20.500 --> 01:22.010
Now I'm certain of something.

01:22.550 --> 01:24.840
There is a way to save everyone.

01:25.150 --> 01:25.850
What?

01:25.850 --> 01:27.510
I told you.

01:27.510 --> 01:30.230
I'm a hero of justice. 
Nothing is impossible for me.

01:30.420 --> 01:31.810
It's right here.

01:32.330 --> 01:34.200
There's something heavier 
than the desk right here.

01:34.200 --> 01:35.060
Wait...

01:35.530 --> 01:38.530
Later, Bra-chan.

01:55.670 --> 01:59.680
<b><i>Twilight Goodbye</i></b>

01:55.930 --> 01:59.090
All units, attack!

02:01.520 --> 02:02.900
<i>I've been waiting...</i>

02:02.900 --> 02:04.230
<i>This is the moment.</i>

02:05.040 --> 02:08.390
<i>There's a slight opening 
in Gen'ichiro's sword.</i>

02:08.830 --> 02:10.890
<i>A weakness that only I know.</i>

02:11.530 --> 02:13.270
<i>What I need is bloodlust...</i>

02:13.670 --> 02:14.850
<i>For the death of my friend.</i>

02:15.320 --> 02:16.260
Prepare yourself!

02:18.790 --> 02:20.140
Tatsumi-ryu style kata:

02:20.780 --> 02:22.230
Ichinotachi!

02:25.660 --> 02:27.590
I knew you would try!

02:48.880 --> 02:50.870
<i>The only way you'll cease to be invincible</i>

02:50.870 --> 02:53.010
<i>is if you let go of your sword!</i>

02:53.960 --> 02:56.060
<i>This is Fukuzawa's best distance.</i>

02:56.410 --> 02:58.350
<i>Grabbing my arm for an over-back throw?</i>

02:59.090 --> 03:00.020
<i>No!</i>

03:00.270 --> 03:01.540
<i>The dagger on the ground!</i>

03:02.750 --> 03:03.480
Wrong!

03:09.990 --> 03:11.560
All units!

03:11.560 --> 03:12.950
Cease your attack!

03:20.590 --> 03:22.660
My, look at this.

03:23.330 --> 03:27.560
A perfect starry night,
 befitting Dazai-kun's end.

03:27.560 --> 03:29.880
Goal!

03:29.880 --> 03:33.680
Fyodor makes it to the
 finish line in first place!

03:33.680 --> 03:35.230
Absolutely fantastic!

03:35.230 --> 03:37.460
My very best friend, everyone!
 So damn awesome!

03:36.840 --> 03:38.830
Save the acclamations, please.

03:39.310 --> 03:40.910
The thing.

03:40.910 --> 03:42.120
The thing?

03:42.120 --> 03:43.490
You mean this?

03:45.020 --> 03:46.620
But first!

03:46.860 --> 03:48.350
May I ask you something?

03:48.820 --> 03:53.450
Dazai-kun was using his pulse to 
encode his messages to the outside.

03:53.450 --> 03:55.760
How were you communicating?

03:56.270 --> 03:58.220
It's simple.

03:58.890 --> 04:00.170
Using them.

04:07.210 --> 04:08.350
I see.

04:08.700 --> 04:11.490
You had accomplices within the 
Mersault security forces.

04:12.030 --> 04:14.470
Now, it's yours.

04:14.780 --> 04:16.250
Indeed.

04:18.600 --> 04:20.190
Aren't you taking the antidote?

04:20.700 --> 04:22.690
I'll take it in the helicopter.

04:32.540 --> 04:35.420
<i>He was able to cause me harm.</i>

04:35.420 --> 04:40.120
<i>Dazai-kun was most definitely my 
greatest foe since that man.</i>

04:41.120 --> 04:42.090
<i>Though...</i>

04:43.290 --> 04:47.270
<i>This slight injury cost him his life.</i>

04:48.010 --> 04:49.880
<i>I suppose he never amounted to much.</i>

04:51.320 --> 04:54.630
I can't pilot the helicopter 
with my injuries.

04:54.630 --> 04:56.580
Please take the stick.

05:02.050 --> 05:04.650
By the way, what became of Sigma-kun?

05:04.960 --> 05:06.650
He was brave.

05:07.310 --> 05:10.180
He'll never awaken again, though.

05:11.010 --> 05:16.090
Those who oppose you always 
meet an untimely demise.

05:17.620 --> 05:19.220
What about you?

05:19.580 --> 05:21.960
What will you do, once you're out of here?

05:21.960 --> 05:24.190
Just as you said.

05:25.120 --> 05:29.420
For starters, you tried to kill me,
 so I'll erase you.

05:31.300 --> 05:32.510
I like it.

05:34.050 --> 05:36.580
It's the beginning of a new game.

05:40.390 --> 05:41.830
Oh, dear.

05:41.830 --> 05:44.610
Do you really want to be treating 
the antidote like that?

05:51.150 --> 05:52.110
Fyodor-kun?

05:56.320 --> 05:58.130
How did this happen?!

05:58.520 --> 06:00.050
What a shame.

06:01.610 --> 06:03.880
I was so close to dying.

06:06.020 --> 06:07.090
But you see...

06:08.500 --> 06:11.340
You can't kill me.

06:20.100 --> 06:23.070
I'm... alive?

06:25.400 --> 06:27.220
Why are you here?

06:27.220 --> 06:29.130
I ordered him here.

06:30.240 --> 06:31.690
Bra-chan!

06:31.690 --> 06:33.290
Your body!

06:33.290 --> 06:36.990
Thanks to your selfless 
efforts to remove the sword.

06:37.330 --> 06:40.220
I am lord and count.

06:43.580 --> 06:48.670
But in this moment, I am your knight.

06:52.860 --> 06:54.300
<i>Invading armies have surrendered!</i>

06:54.590 --> 06:56.050
<i>They're retreating!</i>

07:02.550 --> 07:06.790
<i>All missiles disabled and descending.</i>

07:11.550 --> 07:12.620
Wake up.

07:18.550 --> 07:19.810
Rampo-san!

07:20.420 --> 07:21.960
It's done.

07:21.960 --> 07:23.940
Everything.

07:26.700 --> 07:28.180
Dazai-kun...

07:28.180 --> 07:29.310
How...

07:29.550 --> 07:33.020
Unlike you, I don't have 
control over all things.

07:33.400 --> 07:36.840
My hand was full of uncertain cards.

07:37.540 --> 07:40.530
But you had one weakness:

07:41.290 --> 07:44.510
You don't trust anything 
you can't manipulate.

07:45.720 --> 07:46.980
Allies.

07:47.650 --> 07:50.820
Bram took back his special 
ability at the airport.

07:50.820 --> 07:56.740
Rampo-san negotiated with him and had him 
take over the vampire piloting the helicopter.

07:57.570 --> 08:00.560
It wasn't anything we could 
have planned ahead of time,

08:00.560 --> 08:04.140
but I trusted that's what 
Rampo-san would do.

08:04.140 --> 08:07.920
But you were shot in the head!

08:07.920 --> 08:09.290
Oh, this?

08:09.720 --> 08:12.120
Yeah, that hurt.

08:12.120 --> 08:14.710
That dumbass was supposed to go easy.

08:14.710 --> 08:16.400
Who are you calling a dumbass?

08:18.640 --> 08:19.860
I see.

08:22.410 --> 08:26.390
Chuuya was never a vampire to begin with.

08:28.270 --> 08:31.890
All units! Cease your attack!

08:31.890 --> 08:33.080
I repeat!

08:35.880 --> 08:38.000
<i>He'll try to take the sword 
and change the past!</i>

08:38.220 --> 08:39.280
You will not!

08:40.490 --> 08:43.910
<i>Free of thought, free of mind, 
free of need, free of self.</i>

08:45.540 --> 08:47.540
<b><i>Tatsumi-Ryu
 Style Kata</i></b>

08:45.550 --> 08:47.200
Tatsumi-ryu style kata:

08:47.770 --> 08:49.250
Ninotachi!

08:50.420 --> 08:57.090
<i>It was the most flawless strike of my life.</i>

08:57.850 --> 09:01.590
<i>Thus, there was no stopping midway.</i>

09:03.090 --> 09:05.450
<i>The moment I saw the look 
on my friend's face,</i>

09:05.450 --> 09:09.320
<i>I understood the truth, and my own error.</i>

09:11.560 --> 09:17.230
<i>But my sword had already cut him down.</i>

09:17.840 --> 09:19.410
Gen'ichiro!

09:20.840 --> 09:22.400
Poe's notebook!

09:22.400 --> 09:23.770
It was stolen?

09:28.950 --> 09:31.540
Freaking hell, it's not coming out.

09:32.050 --> 09:34.070
Wretched boss glued it in!

09:34.390 --> 09:36.300
It was all an act.

09:36.900 --> 09:40.620
I was only able to get out of the elevator

09:41.050 --> 09:44.480
because Chuuya manipulated gravity.

09:47.730 --> 09:50.980
And then, Chuuya shoots me in the head.

09:51.300 --> 09:53.490
The bullet stops at my skull.

09:53.810 --> 09:57.170
We used to do this all the time, remember?

09:57.170 --> 09:58.390
Suck it!

09:58.760 --> 10:02.030
You couldn't see how fast the bullet was 
traveling through the security camera.

10:02.450 --> 10:07.910
Also, the water attack was only to distract 
you from my actual goals, you see.

10:08.610 --> 10:10.550
Your actual goal?

10:10.550 --> 10:12.300
That wound.

10:13.390 --> 10:18.270
With your hand injured, you'd have no choice 
but to let the vampire take the cockpit.

10:18.770 --> 10:20.030
And...

10:23.930 --> 10:24.940
Wait!

10:25.820 --> 10:28.930
Goodbye, Fyodor.

10:40.460 --> 10:44.460
Eli, Eli, lama sabachtani?

11:02.940 --> 11:04.820
Good memories.

11:04.820 --> 11:06.760
We're in Poe's novel space.

11:08.200 --> 11:11.280
I've done all I ought to have done.

11:11.980 --> 11:12.730
Yeah.

11:14.040 --> 11:16.610
You win, Gen'ichiro.

11:17.160 --> 11:22.670
Today is the day UN Security Council 
Resolution 2415 will be voted on.

11:23.150 --> 11:27.270
It will have a special amendment such 
that a command structure is formed

11:27.270 --> 11:31.800
overriding the command of 
each nation's militaries,

11:31.800 --> 11:34.140
so as to prevent incidents like today's.

11:34.340 --> 11:37.780
The commander in chief 
will hold the One Order.

11:38.250 --> 11:41.160
A single individual will take
 command over all the world's forces.

11:41.160 --> 11:42.100
That's right.

11:42.730 --> 11:46.260
But it won't be to dominate the world.

11:48.370 --> 11:50.070
Your goal...

11:51.520 --> 11:54.280
Was to rid the world of war.

11:58.950 --> 12:00.370
Please be careful.

12:01.930 --> 12:04.510
The drug is still in your system.

12:08.150 --> 12:09.480
Weren't we..

12:09.480 --> 12:12.100
We were attacked by Fukuzawa from behind.

12:12.710 --> 12:14.960
Your wounds have already been treated.

12:15.460 --> 12:17.750
This device was set so that

12:17.750 --> 12:20.720
you would be brought back without 
your injuries once it was unplugged.

12:22.060 --> 12:25.550
This is the weight of 36 years.

12:26.580 --> 12:28.540
Thirty-six years later.

12:29.190 --> 12:32.430
One day, I received a message 
through the Amenogozen.

12:32.690 --> 12:37.740
It was a prophecy of a world war 
that would happen in 36 years.

12:38.790 --> 12:41.360
It said it would be sparked by 
a multinational conflict,

12:41.360 --> 12:47.440
and advanced autonomous weapons and
 bioweapons would take 210 million lives.

12:49.070 --> 12:50.280
Fukuzawa...

12:52.490 --> 12:54.140
What would you do?

12:55.210 --> 12:58.390
So, is that anemic jackass dead?

12:58.680 --> 13:00.010
Yeah.

13:00.010 --> 13:02.390
Fyodor's no doubt dead.

13:02.900 --> 13:03.980
I see.

13:06.170 --> 13:07.900
Congrats, Nikolai.

13:08.250 --> 13:10.590
You wanted to kill him, didn't you?

13:10.910 --> 13:11.860
Yeah.

13:11.860 --> 13:13.350
I certainly did.

13:13.350 --> 13:15.170
No, I didn't.

13:15.820 --> 13:16.810
No...

13:16.810 --> 13:18.030
You're right.

13:18.970 --> 13:22.330
I never exchanged many 
words with Fyodor-kun.

13:22.940 --> 13:30.120
But my life since I met him felt 
nothing like it did prior.

13:31.260 --> 13:33.060
Fyodor-kun was right.

13:33.060 --> 13:35.580
I fought so I could lose myself.

13:37.650 --> 13:39.550
Now, I...

13:40.550 --> 13:43.040
What happened to your usual snark?

13:43.350 --> 13:44.200
Nah.

13:44.740 --> 13:46.340
Not today.

13:46.820 --> 13:48.850
I got the antidote, too.

13:50.770 --> 13:52.170
Fukuzawa...

13:52.170 --> 13:54.050
Why does war happen?

13:54.280 --> 13:56.470
The reason for war?

13:56.470 --> 13:57.240
Yeah.

13:58.450 --> 14:00.620
Long ago, in the warring states period,

14:00.620 --> 14:04.420
domains warred with each other 
and people killed one another.

14:05.070 --> 14:10.020
But is there any chance that one prefecture 
would go to war with another in modern times?

14:10.790 --> 14:11.840
Not at all.

14:12.350 --> 14:16.370
Long ago, each domain was sovereign, 
with separate powers from the rest.

14:16.370 --> 14:18.460
They were <i>others</i>.

14:18.460 --> 14:22.360
But adjacent prefectures can intermingle, 
and are peer organizations.

14:21.400 --> 14:31.180
<b>Map of Japan</b>

14:22.360 --> 14:24.630
Each is a <i>we</i>.

14:25.490 --> 14:30.910
You're saying that wars can only ever 
happen between a <i>them</i> and an <i>us</i>.

14:31.420 --> 14:36.100
Thus, in the far future, with the development
 of communication and transportation,

14:36.100 --> 14:42.090
all people will become a <i>we</i>, 
and war will fade away on its own.

14:42.940 --> 14:45.240
But I can't wait that long.

14:45.850 --> 14:50.950
Even if only by a year sooner, I want to 
cleanse this world of war—of the hell that it is.

14:51.260 --> 14:56.240
Thus, I chose to make all of humanity a <i>we</i>.

14:56.510 --> 14:59.370
Your "destruction of the state."

15:13.390 --> 15:16.340
I remember you had stolen those kintons.

15:16.850 --> 15:19.670
You ate them, too. You're equally guilty.

15:19.670 --> 15:20.900
You coward.

15:21.300 --> 15:23.170
You served it with hojicha tea.

15:23.170 --> 15:24.310
How could I resist?

15:29.130 --> 15:30.630
Listen, Gen'ichiro...

15:31.180 --> 15:33.430
Uniting humanity is impossible.

15:34.030 --> 15:37.110
You can't turn hundreds of 
nations into one overnight.

15:37.600 --> 15:40.150
The need for integrity is a limiting factor.

15:40.650 --> 15:43.200
I have no doubt you're aware of that.

15:43.200 --> 15:47.590
Then let me ask you, Fukuzawa.
 What is a state?

15:48.730 --> 15:53.200
In crude terms, a state is an 
entity that has a right to violence.

15:53.200 --> 15:56.760
Invariably, the state authorizes 
any necessary violence.

15:57.090 --> 16:00.770
You, in the Detective Agency, 
carry guns, too, do you not?

16:03.180 --> 16:06.570
If the leader of the Army of 
Mankind uses the One Order,

16:06.570 --> 16:09.920
every nation in the world loses 
its foundation of sovereignty.

16:10.460 --> 16:14.980
With every army under the umbrella of the 
Army of Mankind, there will be no war.

16:16.320 --> 16:18.440
And thus the terror plot!

16:19.200 --> 16:22.690
All to make the Army of Mankind 
and the One Order your own.

16:23.440 --> 16:27.250
The world will soon form a supernation, 
a federation of humanity,

16:27.250 --> 16:30.210
headed by the chief commander 
of the Army of Mankind.

16:30.430 --> 16:34.340
With those preparations complete, 
the page will take effect.

16:34.340 --> 16:40.160
Reality will be amended, and none will 
question the need to unify humanity.

16:40.750 --> 16:42.630
War itself will cease to exist.

16:43.560 --> 16:45.080
Forever.

16:47.700 --> 16:49.110
Gen'ichiro...

16:49.110 --> 16:51.050
That's never going to happen.

16:51.050 --> 16:56.690
Even with war gone, all that remains 
is the dictatorship of one.

16:57.130 --> 17:02.210
And as history has demonstrated, 
absolute power corrupts absolutely.

17:02.210 --> 17:03.830
That's right.

17:03.830 --> 17:07.520
That's why I had to make you use it.

17:08.520 --> 17:10.310
All units!

17:10.310 --> 17:11.670
Cease your attack!

17:14.540 --> 17:18.700
Do you know why the 
One Order obeyed you?

17:22.650 --> 17:24.580
Cut down my head.

17:25.770 --> 17:27.960
Become the chief commander 
of the Army of Mankind

17:27.960 --> 17:29.800
and the hero who stops the terror attack.

17:30.690 --> 17:35.240
It was always configured 
to respond to my voice?

17:35.850 --> 17:40.110
I placed a certain condition 
on the terror plot.

17:41.230 --> 17:44.560
I would sacrifice no more than 500 lives.

17:44.560 --> 17:45.710
Five hundred!

17:46.240 --> 17:48.040
That is the cost of peace.

17:48.430 --> 17:53.260
The price to pay to save the 210 million lives 
that would be lost in the coming war.

17:54.930 --> 17:56.970
Would you call that a bad deal?

17:59.540 --> 18:01.620
The proposal was Fyodor's.

18:02.080 --> 18:04.030
No one else could have done it.

18:04.030 --> 18:04.800
That's it.

18:05.390 --> 18:08.560
You must be aware of how evil he is.

18:08.560 --> 18:11.640
That's why I had him stay in prison.

18:11.640 --> 18:15.470
Not even he could have managed to
 meddle from the other side of the planet.

18:16.210 --> 18:17.310
Fukuzawa...

18:17.690 --> 18:19.060
Kill me!

18:19.610 --> 18:22.270
You are to become the chief commander
 of the Army of Mankind.

18:22.270 --> 18:24.680
There is no other way to 
save the Detective Agency.

18:25.240 --> 18:27.890
My life, or the Detective Agency.

18:28.360 --> 18:29.080
Choose!

18:46.850 --> 18:49.440
We've left the novel world.

18:49.440 --> 18:50.580
Good.

18:51.360 --> 18:55.140
The moment of evil's beheading 
must be witnessed.

18:57.240 --> 18:58.850
Any regrets?

19:00.150 --> 19:00.870
None.

19:11.400 --> 19:16.970
Say, Fukuzawa, if you could have just one 
wish granted, what would you wish for?

19:17.200 --> 19:18.980
Let's see...

19:18.980 --> 19:21.860
I would wish for the strength 
to protect those closest to me.

19:22.980 --> 19:23.880
You?

19:24.460 --> 19:27.130
I would wish for world peace.

19:30.770 --> 19:31.750
I'm sorry.

19:32.120 --> 19:33.070
I can't do it.

19:35.580 --> 19:36.760
It's fine.

19:37.990 --> 19:39.630
I suspected as much.

19:46.300 --> 19:48.750
I'm sorry, Teruko-kun.

19:49.030 --> 19:50.650
You're a coward!

19:50.650 --> 19:52.090
This isn't fair!

19:52.090 --> 19:54.090
You knew how I felt!

19:58.700 --> 20:02.330
You killed him. That's your line.

20:02.330 --> 20:04.020
Otherwise, I'll make you regret it!

20:04.020 --> 20:06.120
Fukuzawa...

20:06.900 --> 20:09.450
Are you there?

20:10.580 --> 20:11.670
Boss!

20:12.330 --> 20:13.590
Boss!

20:14.060 --> 20:15.450
Stay back, kid!

20:17.250 --> 20:18.370
Don't look at him!

20:18.370 --> 20:18.900
But...

20:21.260 --> 20:22.790
Please don't do this to him.

20:39.190 --> 20:41.790
I'm a little tired.

20:42.510 --> 20:44.300
Rest up.

20:44.760 --> 20:47.690
I would wish for world peace.

20:48.830 --> 20:51.380
Was there no other way?

21:31.010 --> 21:33.760
<i>When the Armed Detective Agency was formed,</i>

21:34.200 --> 21:38.550
<i>the first guest at our 
celebration was this man.</i>

21:40.180 --> 21:44.490
He must be a little lonely,
now that I've found my own path.

21:45.690 --> 21:48.320
<i>That must not be all.</i>

21:49.090 --> 21:52.920
You ought to decide what 
happens to this, boss.

22:15.060 --> 22:16.000
<i>Yes.</i>

22:16.560 --> 22:18.480
<i>You can't destroy it.</i>

22:19.290 --> 22:25.450
<i>That, Fukuzawa-san, is the curse 
that the old man placed on you.</i>

22:32.490 --> 22:36.370
<b>Two hours later</b>

23:02.730 --> 23:03.950
Akutagawa!

23:07.830 --> 23:11.960
We're concluding this story 
started by Fukuchi Ouchi.

23:13.090 --> 23:14.610
Just the two of us?

23:15.510 --> 23:17.130
Do we need any more?

23:23.100 --> 23:24.760
Let's go, Akutagawa!

23:36.270 --> 23:39.970
<b><i>To Be Continued</i></b>
